			OSQL
	      ORACLE Visual SQL Query Tool

---------------------------------------------------------------
		    Results Window
---------------------------------------------------------------

  -Title Bar-
  Each results window is titled "OSQL Result [resultno]",
  where:

  	[resultno]	=	Unique execution number.

  -Query Area-
  The query that was executed can be displayed in a scrollable
  text window.  Above the query window to the right is a 
  "Show/Hide Query" button and a  "Save Query" button.  The
  "Show/Hide Query" button allows the user to alternately show
  or hide the SQL text that generated the results.  The "Save
  Query" button allows the user to save the query to a file.
  Osql defaults to hiding the SQL query text unless the user
  sets the default to "Show" on the Results Query Window sub-
  menu of the %%
  hyperhelp_link "Props" Osql.menu Props %% menu.

  -Paned Area Adjustor-
  Below the Query Area is a separator containing a black spot
  that can be used to adjust the total area consumed by the 
  Query Area relative to the Results Area.  By placing the
  mouse pointer on the black spot and depressing and dragging
  the pointer up or down, the relative vertical sizes of the
  Query and Results areas will be adjusted.

  -Results Area-
  Results are displayed in a three-part, horizontally and
  vertically scrollable listbox.  The column names of the
  returned elements are in a row at the top of the Results
  Area.  Along the left side are the numbers of the returned
  rows.  In the center listbox are the column values for each
  row.

  The listbox is titled with the result number, number of rows
  returned and the number of seconds elapsed time to execute the
  query.

  An optional button will be shown below the results listbox
  when the user has displayed objects using the %%
  hyperhelp_link "Objects" Osql.menu Objects%% button
  of the %%
  hyperhelp_link "menu bar" Osql.menu%%.  This button will be activated if there are
  results rows.  When active, the user may select a row in the
  listbox, press the optional button, and see additional
  information about the selected object.

  A row of command buttons below the listbox provides for the
  following actions:

	Button		Action
	-------		-------
	
  	Ok		Dismiss the results window.

  	Print		Print the results acording to the
  			current print command.  The print
  			command can be set using the "Print"
  			option of the %%
  			hyperhelp_link "Props" Osql.menu Props%% menu.

  	Save		Save the results into a file.

  	Search		Enter a text string to search the
  			results for.

  	Next		Search for the next occurrence of
  			the current search string.


  NOTE:

  Resizing a Results Window sets the size for subsequent
  results windows.
  